From a0b0bcaf6d1d3474081bd7b1c836df67e98870a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JoshuaHayesWasHere <josh.hayes121@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:19:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): jstack tree root rows drag to a new place within
 the active and the idle group

A root row drags by mouse to a new place in its own group, active or idle, and Alt+ArrowUp and
Alt+ArrowDown (or Move up and Move down in its menu) move it one place. It never crosses the
divider: which group a root is in stays automatic, and "No project" stays pinned last. While it
is dragged, the root folds to its own row and shows at the place it would drop at; Escape puts
it back.

The order is the projects' order (`projectOrder`), written through the UI state's
`reorderProjects`, which keeps it in localStorage across a reload. It is ranked before the
split, so a root that turns active or idle keeps its rank among the others, and a project never
dragged follows the ranked ones in the sidebar's order.
